{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The locking nuts connect to my recent interest in screws and locking washers because they help keep fastened parts secure, although I would skip this particular SAE kit.",
    "Fastening hardware reflects part of what I have been shopping for recently: small fasteners and magnetic mounting hooks."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The half-inch washers are much larger than my recent M3–M5 screws, and the SAE nuts do not match those metric sizes; a similar purpose does not make them compatible.",
    "Cleaners, inspection cameras, cutting wheels, wire connectors, tubing and hose clamps serve tasks I am not currently doing, even though they might belong in the same workshop.",
    "Epoxy and super glue do not follow from my current fastening needs, and ten containers of glue would be excessive for my occasional use."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop or repair supply, rather than the particular fastening and mounting tasks behind them.",
    "Items that secure or join things seem to have been treated as interchangeable, despite differences between magnetic hooks, threaded fasteners, adhesives, hose clamps and wire splices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Metric sizing and compatibility matter: my recent screw assortment was M3–M5, so locking hardware needs to fit those screws to be useful.",
    "My recent purchases cluster around small fasteners and magnetic hooks, which gives me more reason to consider related mounting supplies than unrelated repair equipment.",
    "I rarely buy without an immediate need, so a broadly useful supply or a large quantity alone is not enough to interest me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in fastening supplies but stretched it into general repair shopping while missing the fit and immediate purpose that determine whether I would buy."
}"}
